I never thought that throwing heavier objects causes you to be pushed 
further away.  Is this true?  If so, I call possible violation of 
Newton laws; it's the impulse I give the object which determines my 
own acceleration, not the weight of the object.  If I throw a wand as 
far as I can (seems like a logical assumption to me that throwing wands 
or such stuff is done "with all your might"), I would naively think that 
this creates roughly the same impulse as when throwing, say, a chest 
full of plate armor as far as I can.  On the other hand, it might be 
true that the human body is capable of creating more impulse when 
throwing heavy objects.  I wonder whether the DevTeam made a field-study 
about this subject before coding the effects.. 

